---
// The Flossify iPhone app (mobile/, a native shell around this website) marks itself in the user agent
// ("FlossifyApp/1", capacitor.config.json). Only then does a page load the app's script (./app-shell.js): haptics, the
// iOS-style page transitions, printing and saving through iOS, and the page's colours behind the status bar. Every
// other visitor runs this one test and nothing else, so the website is unchanged in a browser. It sits in the head of
// every layout and of every page with its own document (the print pages, the signing page), before any script that
// might call print().
//
// The script is served from a hashed, immutable address (/assets/…), so a phone loads it once per release and never
// waits on the network for it again (it blocks the page's parsing, by design: it must run before the page's own
// scripts). Patients' phones have no service worker; this is what keeps a bad line from holding their pages.
import shell from './app-shell.js?url';
---
<script is:inline define:vars={{ shell }}>
  if (/\bFlossifyApp\//.test(navigator.userAgent)) {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-app', '');
    document.write('<script src="' + shell + '"><\/script>');
  }
</script>
